critical  code-injection.controlled  .github/workflows/env.yml:8:24
  env.TITLE is written into the run script by ${{ }}, and an attacker controls it on issues
  impact: the value becomes code
    8 |       - run: echo "${{ env.TITLE }}"
      |                        ^^^^^^^^^
    .github/workflows/env.yml:6:14  env.TITLE gets its value here
    6 |       TITLE: ${{ github.event.issue.title }}
      |              ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  remedy: pass it through env and read the variable
  fix (review): move the expressions of the step an attacker controls into its env (1 edits)  [--fix=review]
    side effect: The value of the ${{ }} expression is no longer parsed by the program that reads the script (the shell, or the JavaScript runtime of actions/github-script) as part of the script text: characters of the value that the program interpreted before the fix (such as $, `, \, double quotes and line breaks) are taken as plain characters, and a workflow that relied on the program interpreting those characters runs differently.

